   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1 PMU established</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">0</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Establish the project office and complete recruitment of staff</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Staff recruitment initiated</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Strengthened KSRLPS state mission with high quality technical assistance and program management capabilities in the field of rural economic transformation towards attaining the mission goals of reducing poverty and empowering the poor rural women
2. Developed detailed value chain development plans and market assessment &amp; business viability studies to address the gaps and forward-backward linkages for various farm related products 
3. Developed key systems and processes for knowledge management, communication, Innovations &amp; Partnership, reveiw, monitoring and evaluation of the programme.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Twenty five skilled professionals have been deployed as Senior Technical Expert (STEs)/State Project Managers(SPMs), Technical Experts (TEs)/Assistant State Project Managers (ASPMs), Deputy Program Managers(DPMs) and Project Associates. They are engaged in the fields of Farm/Non-Farm livelihoods, Digital finance, Social management framework &amp; Gender, Insurance &amp; Pension and Cluster Level Federation (CLF) strengthening. Three skilled social sector professionals at the district level as District Technical Expert (DTEs) and 78 Block Coordinators (BCs) at block level in the fields of livelihood development and social and financial inclusion have also been deployed ensuring strengthening of SRLM state mission and on ground implementation. Out of the 108 IC positions 81 IC positions are currently engaged. 

2. A detailed value chain analysis was carried out in three NRETP districts, Tumkur, Gadag and Uttarakannada. Through this study value chain mapping and analysis of 8 major agriculture and horticulture commodities and livelihood practices of these three districts were completed. Business plans for these commodities have been prepared and actionable interventions suggested to increase incomes of women producer groups and rural women owned enterprises.

3. Online Registry for SHG Enterprise and Artisan Santhe Kaushalkar has been developed, 2000+ products and 1000+ entrepreneurs/artisans have been onboarded on Santhe Kaushalkar platform. The Santhe Kaushalkar platform has been handed over to SRLM for statewide rollout. 
Partnership development activities such as NGO Conclave have been executed where 25+ organizations participated resulting in MoUs between organizations and SRLM, further partnership building activities such as linking with Ecommerce platforms has been executed.
Expertise has been lent in activities such as developing the Krishi Udyog Sakhi curriculum and training. A pipeline of field stories and case studies was developed and a success story from the field was featured on the UNDP blog.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Strengthened KSRLPS state mission with high quality technical assistance and program management capabilities in the field of rural economic transformation towards attaining the mission goals of reducing poverty and empowering the poor rural women

2. Developed a professional support and service delivery architecture at the grass root level ensuring sustainable livelihood enhancements and improved access to financial services through establishing efficient and effective institutional platforms of the rural poor.

3. Developed key systems and processes for knowledge management, communication, Innovations &amp; Partnership, reveiw, monitoring and evaluation of the programme.

4. Developed detailed value chain development plans and market assessment &amp; business viability studies to address the gaps and forward-backward linkages for various farm related products</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Project Management Unit at Bangalore with 18 members established and 7 more placement is in progress.
2. 3 district level functionaries and 65 bock level functionaries are placed. the selection of the remaining 13 team members at the block level is in progress. 
3. The following activities are in progress, 
        &#x2022;Santhe Kaushalkar &#x2013; SHG and Artisan profiling platform developed and handed over to KSRLPS. 
        &#x2022;14 different product categories and 86 subcategories defined and 993 product templates developed. 
        &#x2022; 46 SHG enterprises and 780 artisans and 67 buyers have registered on the platform.
        &#x2022; 912 KSRLPS field functionaries have been trained on using the platform. 
        &#x2022; 396 products of SHG enterprises/artisans have been uploaded on the platform by SHG enterprises/artisans. 
4. We are undertaking a holistic value chain study of high value farm and non-farm commodities in 10 blocks. We have floated the RFP for the study and shortly we will onboard a technical agency to implement the project.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
